Build Dawn for HarmonyOS, so WebGPU has a decoder to run on.

use_dawn left OHOS out, so the GPU process had no WebGPU decoder and
every WebGPU context failed ("Failed to create WebGPU Context Provider")
even with --enable-unsafe-webgpu. Dawn's Vulkan backend then needs the loader by the
name HarmonyOS gives it, libvulkan.so, as on Android; OHOS is otherwise
taken for Linux there, which looks for libvulkan.so.1.

Then, still on OHOS only: Dawn's Vulkan backend is built (dawn_enable_vulkan)
with the Linux external memory and semaphore services its C++ calls, since
OHOS compiles as Linux there; adapters are taken although they cannot import
Linux-style external memory; and a WebGPU canvas's textures are GL textures
reaching Dawn through DawnFallbackImageRepresentation's copies -- nothing
here shares memory between Dawn's Vulkan device and the GL compositor.

Experimental and behind --enable-unsafe-webgpu: on a Mate 70 Pro+ the
Maleoon 920 adapter is found and WebGPU samples draw, through CPU copies.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 (Dawn 8597a1aaec54).

